C++ Loop Benchmark

This is a simple C++ program I made to test how long it takes for a loop to run 1,000,000 times.

About the Program

The program uses a "for" loop and a counter. It also uses the "<chrono>" library to measure the time taken by the loop.

It shows:

- Number of iterations
- Final count
- Execution time in milliseconds

What I Used

- C++
- Code::Blocks
- "<iostream>"
- "<chrono>"

The execution time can be different every time I run the program because it depends on the computer's current performance and what other programs are running.

What I Learned

From this activity, I learned how to use a "for" loop for a large number of iterations and how to measure the execution time of a program using "<chrono>". I also learned that the execution time is not always the same every time the program runs.
